{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Aaron shall make atonement on its horns once a year.</b> To make atonement for what is said (Psalms 75:6): ״אַל תָּרִימוּ לַמָּרוֹם קַרְנְכֶם״ ('Lift not up your horn on high'), as explained above concerning the bronze altar. 'Once a year' etc. — for on that very day man is made as clean as the ministering angels from sin, and the soul returns to its purity as in days of old and years of antiquity; and the discerning will hear and add instruction."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:24:16.197291078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}